  ],
  "excerpt": "[docs/resource-guides/onprem/storage.md#on-premises-storage-type-storage]\nRun functions when files appear in a bucket, and read or write objects: the host's built-in buckets, a shared folder, MinIO or another S3-compatible store, or a bucket in a cloud (S3, R2, Azure Blob, GCS, ...). The host lists each watched bucket every `poll_seconds` and compares ETags: a new or changed object emits `created`, a missing one `deleted`. Objects already there at the first start are recorded, not emitted.",
  "provider": "ibm",
  "stage": "prod",
  "mode": "ask",
  "page": "Overview",
  "multi_turn": false
 },
